Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: reserve GPU firmware memory on hamoa

The working linux-sp11 reference at d6333a45f9bc reserves gpu-prr and
pld-gmu as no-map ranges in hamoa.dtsi. Restore these two GPU-related
ranges from the reference; the v7.3 base and the compiled M15 DTB omit
them. Their role in the observed reset remains unproven.

Compare the EFI memory map and /proc/iomem before and after on the same
device, check for reservation conflicts, and confirm that the clean
GPU-on debug entry no longer resets. Reject the candidate for no change,
a regression, a reservation conflict, or a continuing GPU reset.

The ranges total 68 KiB. If UEFI already reserves them, no additional
RAM should be lost; otherwise up to 68 KiB may become unavailable.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index 8a96ea1..24c4c94 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -545,6 +545,16 @@ secdata_apss_mem: secdata-apss@81cff000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		gpu_prr_mem: gpu-prr@81f00000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x81f00000 0x0 0x10000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		pld_gmu_mem: pld-gmu@81f36000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x81f36000 0x0 0x1000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		adsp_rpc_remote_heap_mem: adsp-rpc-remote-heap@84b00000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0x84b00000 0x0 0x800000>;
 			no-map;
